---
name: Org KPI Key Normalization
description: Canonical owner/KPI key normalization helper and tiered overwrite policy for Org KPI propagation
type: feature
---
All joins on `(category_id, kra_name, kpi_name)` between `kpis`, `org_kpi_data_owners`, and `org_kpi_values` MUST use `normalizeKpiKey` from `src/lib/orgKpiKey.ts` (lowercase + `\r` strip + `\s+`-collapse + trim). Never re-implement inline.

Propagation overwrite policy (`propagate_org_kpi_value.p_overwrite_policy`):
- `safe` — legacy, only `kra_set`
- `pre_review_only` (default) — also `self_review` rows
- `force_pre_terminal` — admin escalation, anything pre-`manager_check`

Every overwrite emits `ORG_KPI_VALUE_OVERWRITTEN` audit. `preview_org_kpi_propagation` mirrors the policy and returns Old→New self_score for the dialog diff.

Reference: ADR-053, ADR-054. Owner-table cleanup snapshotted to `org_kpi_owner_key_backup` (admin-read RLS).
## RLS predicates (ADR-057, May 2026)

Any RLS policy that joins on the org-KPI triple `(category_id, kra_name, kpi_name)` MUST wrap `kra_name` and `kpi_name` in `public.normalize_kpi_text(...)` on **both** sides of the comparison. Strict `=` is forbidden — owner-table rows and `kpis`/`org_kpi_values` rows can drift by case, embedded `\r`, or collapsed whitespace.

Helper contract (must stay in sync with JS `normalizeText` in `src/lib/orgKpiKey.ts`):
`btrim(regexp_replace(replace(lower(coalesce(p,'')), E'\r',''), '\s+',' ','g'))`

Affected policies brought into compliance:
- `kpis` → "Data owners can view assigned org-level KPIs"
- `org_kpi_values` → "Data owners can insert their assigned org_kpi_values"
- `org_kpi_values` → "Data owners can update their assigned org_kpi_values"

Backup of pre-canonicalization owner rows: `org_kpi_owner_key_backup_2026_05` (admin-read RLS).
Parity test: `src/test/orgKpiOwnerNormalization.test.ts`.
